      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Hey there! Great idea and write up. In an upcoming release (hopefully in a couple of weeks) there's a new feature called \"user status\" that aims to address this very issue and a few other ones. Users can set custom status state and even a message that their friends can see. Green - \"join me\" which provides auto reply with an invite when someone \"requests invite\". Yellow - \"active\" which means you are open to invite requests but manually replying. Red \"busy\" which turns off your notifications and lets people know you probably won't reply. Also users can type in a short custom text message that any friend can view. Public users will only see the default color and status message. \n\nI was just testing it this week with the VRChat crew and it works pretty good. We've taked internally before about canned quick replies and maybe get to that too someday. For now this should hopefully help. : )",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
